💔 Hello! I want to tell you a little about the breakdown system in The Last World 🎮 game.

All buildings, units and drones (objects) will be subject to breaking. All these objects will have a parameter - Durability (durab). The durab parameter is different from the health parameter. Durab affects only the performance of objects. However, with a critically low durab indicator, the object will receive health damage.

Each object has its own base durab and can also have its own durability coeff, which determines how much durab damage it will receive from external factors. The durab coeff depends on the object itself, its sizes, materials, technologies. The higher the ratio, the more damage it will take.

The following factors influence the change in durab:
1) Ambient temperature - objects take damage every hour (damage is highly dependent on temperature);
2) Weather conditions - just some of them, for example, a sandstorm;
3) Time or aging - every cycle (day + night) objects receive damage (damage is approximately 0.1% of the base durab, this is approximately 1000 cycles);
4) Random factors, such as a short circuit or technical breakdown, which are random in nature;

How breakdowns appear:
1) Upon reaching 0 durab, the object becomes completely inoperable;
2) Upon reaching the minimum durab threshold, the object may show signs of breakdowns - leakage (typical for buildings), sparks, explosion?
3) For units and drones - reduced movement speed;
4) For buildings - change in the indicator of consumption/production of electricity;
5) For buildings - change in the indicator of the production of components (the time may increase or the component will not be produced at all);
6) For buildings - changing the resource cleaning indicator (the time may increase or the resource will not be cleaned at all);

If you have any suggestions to improve this system, write in the comments or in Discord.

Kind Regards,
Semyon Erochin

